build/
.DS_Store

# ⚠⚠ NEVER COMMIT THESE. Purged from history 2026-09-23 before this repo went
# public. logs/ carry real Bluetooth device addresses; docs/source/ holds captured
# system state -- Apple System Profiler reports and ioreg dumps with the machine's
# hardware serial number. Both are kept locally and backed up; neither belongs on
# GitHub. Re-adding either is how the purge gets silently undone.
logs/
docs/source/

# ⚠⚠ THE SCRUB LIST ITSELF. .scrub-identifiers holds the REAL device addresses that
# sync-to-github.sh scans the public export FOR. A scanner must never publish the thing
# it scans for, so the list is gitignored exactly as airport-extreme does it.
#
# ⚠ IT IS THEREFORE NOT IN THE BACKUP BUNDLES EITHER. An earlier version of this comment
# claimed it was "kept locally and in the Pi backup bundles", which is wrong: a git bundle
# carries committed objects, so a gitignored file is in none of them. It exists on this
# disk and nowhere else. Losing it does not lose anything secret -- the addresses are
# recoverable from the devices themselves and from logs/ -- but it DOES disable the
# publication gate until it is rebuilt, and sync-to-github.sh refuses --push without it,
# which is the safe direction for that failure to point.
.scrub-identifiers
